{"id":"00000001794732494451:148b6ee4b3bdd233ee137968bdcbaf01","text":"Directed b67657 on 2026-11-15T08:44Z with Nate voice direction (physical iPhone off-limits per t-mwgo0adg-1a4n0; sim/beast only): (1) BunRuntime.cpp JSI fast paths (JSValueIsArray instead of global Array.isArray lookup+call; HostFunctionMetadata::call avoiding createObject(nullptr) JSObjectMake + stack borrowed PointerValues for args; JSCRuntime::size direct length prop; stack buffers instead of std::string heap copies on PropNameID/String); (2) typed-packages expansion (ReactFabric-prod + Tamagui + Navigation + LegendList in prod mode, Rolldown CJS fix); (3) BUN_JSC_* GC/heap/JIT throughput tuning; (4) alternating simulator benchmarks + 0.25-core LegendList re-capture -> PR -> One 2.18.1 patch."}
{"id":"00000001794733820480:1066381bd9d0cb31334c70358b086c8e","text":"b67657 jsibench (TESTED, simulator, JIT off, alternating): JSValueIsArray returns 0 for new Proxy([], {}), so isArray keeps the cached Array.isArray fallback (non-array 36 ns vs 450 before). getPropertyNames via one JSObjectMakeArray plus 256-byte utf8 stack buffer: raw props walk 2.75 to 1.85 us, createFromAscii 80 to 52 ns, committed f02702545 on perf/bun-runtime-throughput. Borrowed host-call args held: an object arg costs about 65 ns over a number arg (2-number host call 155 ns, 3-object 355 ns); will take it only if the LegendList scroll bench shows host calls matter. Next: 2,000-item mixed LegendList mount+scroll bench under cpulimit 25% on simulator, Hermes vs Bun."}
{"id":"00000001794735605009:a16054226d1ea5c74df91b4bca8de331","text":"b67657 TM feed bench (TESTED, sim 8CCC71C9, cpulimit 25% from feed mount, bun JIT off, 4 alternating runs, medians): fast scroll 120px x300 frames Hermes 8.8 s vs Bun 5.9 s, frames>33ms 58 vs 18; heavy (drawDistance 2500, ~1000 views) Hermes 18.8 s vs Bun 7.5 s, p95 226 vs 76 ms, mount 159 vs 100 ms. Typed and unlowered within noise of untyped lowered Bun, so both stay out of the 2.18.1 PR. Harness: /Volumes/Mini-1TB/.scratch/bun-aot-rn/tm-bench feed-*.sh, BenchFeed*.native.tsx. Next: one-basic 2.18.0 vs 2.18.1 runtime on engine 0.1.3."}
{"id":"00000001794738089140:3fbae0139d7b46be7ff6ef08fad700bb","text":"b67657 profile decomposition (TESTED, sample at full CPU, heavy feed scroll, busy samples per thread): JS-thread engine time Hermes 1358 (hermesvm) vs Bun 466 (AOT 320 + JSC runtime 146), typed 433, so Bun runs this feed's JS 2.9x faster (3.1x typed). Process busy Hermes 3082 vs Bun 2105: Bun's main thread (1161, UIKit mount) now exceeds its JS thread (868), and cpulimit caps the whole process, which caps scroll gains near 1.5-2.5x and hides typing (7% of engine = 1.6% of process). 25% of the main thread (294 samples) is RN 0.88 ScrollView _remountChildren walking every subview with convertRect on each mount transaction unless enableViewCulling is on (shared cost, both engines). Bun JSI lock churn: C API calls inside host functions take the full JSC lock (callbacks run with locks dropped); protect/unprotect from makeObjectValue/invalidate about 35 samples. In progress: direct JSC value encoding in createValue/valueRef (no lock for numbers/bools/null/undefined, object args 3 locks to 1), round trips verified for 24 value kinds in jsibench; memoized rolldown __toCommonJS A/B on TM feed; one-basic regenerated on main for old/head/work runtime comparison."}
{"id":"00000001794742771994:17691a544d3b8348fd681dcf33bfbbd9","text":"b67657: PR https://github.com/onejs/one/pull/1239 opened (b541ebd83). Direct JSC value encoding committed (host calls -20 to -22% in jsibench). App level within noise: one-basic feed scroll Hermes 7.00 s, Bun old 6.05 s, Bun PR 6.01 s. Memoized rolldown __toCommonJS measured within noise on both engines on the TM feed (heavy: Bun 7.31 vs 7.48 s, Hermes 14.2 vs 14.1 s) and touches the Hermes path, so dropped; patch saved at /Volumes/Mini-1TB/.scratch/bun-aot-rn/memoize-toCommonJS.patch."}
{"id":"00000001794743888188:568ccb3a7ac10530c3e5bd50d975ec82","text":"b67657 TESTED re-render bench (TM app, sim, full CPU, 35 Tamagui feed rows re-rendered via context 60x, unchanged output, 6 alternating runs, median per update): Hermes 25.1 ms, Bun 6.3 ms (4.0x), Bun typed 5.6 ms (4.5x, typed -11%); ranges disjoint vs Hermes. Harness: bench-prelude.js updatePhase, --bench-updates N, BenchFeed*.native.tsx Version context."}
{"id":"00000001794744360955:29cffc24acc6db4ed69ae6b8b05efdd4","text":"Re-render bench (35 Tamagui rows re-render via context, unchanged output, 100% CPU): Hermes vs Bun 4.0x, Bun typed 4.5x (typed 11% over untyped). JSC profile of Bun re-render: React context propagation ~15% (bench artifact), rolldown __copyProps ~8% from RN lazy getters (memo gated to Bun prod builds now being A/B'd), Tamagui discoverMountedHosts ~5%. FINDING for Tamagui lane (INFERRED from source + profile, disprove by profiling with discover mode off): @tamagui/web 3.0.0-0.canary.1792046056862 dist/esm/helpers/nativeStyleEngine.native.js nativeStyleMountMode() sets needsDiscover and queues an idle flush on every render in discover mode; flushNativeStyleLinks then runs discoverMountedHosts, a full fiber-tree DFS up to 1e5 fibers, after each update."}
{"id":"00000001794746605037:1bd16986d4a5ff65ad57a2641e9788c0","text":"Landed on PR #1239: 396bdcb5c memoizes rolldown __toCommonJS in Bun release bundles only (gated !dev && isBunIosEngine). TESTED: TM re-render bench, 12+8 alternating runs, median update time 7-9% lower, scroll unchanged. View culling experiment (local probe, RN enableViewCulling via dangerouslyForceOverride): TESTED in one-basic heavy scroll 25% CPU, 8 runs each: culling removes the ScrollView clip walk (main thread busy 806 -> 722 samples) but scroll time moves only 3-6% (Hermes 7.58->7.10 s, Bun 6.40->6.22 s), inside noise. Not worth a product change now."}
{"id":"00000001794750908643:ec12d6dad8df99cd3f9cd55c35060760","text":"JSC GC tuning TESTED (TM re-render bench, full CPU, JIT off, alternating): useConcurrentGC=false makes heavy scroll worse (6.94 -> 7.94 s at 25% CPU); largeHeapSize 64/128/256 MB shows no re-render gain over 10 runs each (331 default vs 321/326/332 ms; an earlier 16-run -10% did not reproduce) and 256 MB costs ~100 MB footprint. Not shipping any GC flag. Footprint at end of bench: Bun 266 MB vs Hermes 278 MB; re-render 60 updates Bun 331 ms vs Hermes 1415 ms (4.3x)."}
{"id":"00000001794751979937:4cb6a397a2b08c5ca7e80931af033471","text":"PR #1239 reviewed (adversarial subagent): fixed in 5d0d92461 a GC hazard in getPropertyNames for >32 keys (fresh JSStrings held only in malloc memory), ascii strings now 8-bit (JSStringCreateWithCharacters made 16-bit), checked isArray/native state/array length inputs, C API fallback for unknown encodings (BigInt32), memo skipped when __reExport is unrecognized. TESTED jsibench 24 kinds round-trip, vitest 178 pass, tsc. Since v2.18.0 main has only fixes, so 2.18.1 fits a patch. PR merge BLOCKED on required review; asked Nate (tm share --question, ask-2181.md) to approve merge + publish 2.18.1."}
